<ul style=3D"line-height:150%"></ul>
<ul style=3D"line-height:150%"></ul>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%"><span style=3D"font-size: 14px;"><em>Renderin=
g of the proposed first lunar hotel. Image credit: GRU Space</em></span><br=
><br></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%; font-weight:bold; font-size:22px">The first l=
unar hotel is now open for reservations&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">With global travel numbers on the rise, somet=
imes it feels as though there are few places on Earth left untapped by swar=
ms of tourists. For a fortunate few of us, however, one off-the-beaten-path=
 destination with out-of-this-world views may soon become an option.&nbsp;<=
/p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">California-based startup GRU Space is buildin=
g a hotel on the moon =E2=80=94 and, as of this week, it=E2=80=99s official=
ly taking reservations for its grand opening, slated for 2032.&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">The top qualification: being astronomically w=
ealthy. Hopeful space guests must put down a deposit of $250k or $1m, depen=
ding on their selection, though the total cost of the stay is <a href=3D"ht=
tps://media.hubspot.com/e3t/Ctc/UB+113/d2q-Vf04/VWDJYV540XgfW62JSGb4FrmqyW7=
TctdS5JmfCPN4nN_c02-ZW0W5BW0B06lZ3pvW4WJhRT1GBFyYW7XsQ5J5jZFGzW4PsDv36fRyS0=
W6r27GY4cPRgkW1BJB8z7ccQ62W8TBMk7583w2JW5ys5R73pPQwrW93TLzH2kwyTxW89rDl71G8=
s1jW6ZFmbD2X8vbFW4Drzp18RZZ1zW4XMy_V2-Qhl4W1vBPR-2Gx13WW1L5Blh7KMRHTW3Bk74X=
2pRvzmW6R2TXb8zKT59W8371wH8C47RgW2mpWhX6r3wgmf2hfW6n04" style=3D"color:#192=
733" data-hs-link-id=3D"0" data-hs-link-id-v2=3D"7kAlFd3i" target=3D"_blank=
">expected</a> to exceed $10m.&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%; font-weight:bold; font-size:18px">The plan</p=
>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">Starting in 2029, the company will lead two l=
unar missions:</p>
<ul style=3D"line-height:150%">
<li aria-level=3D"1">Mission I will involve: launching a small payload, inc=
luding an inflatable structure that will demonstrate the material intended =
to eventually be used in the hotel=E2=80=99s construction, and testing deve=
lopment of =E2=80=9Cmoon bricks=E2=80=9D using lunar regoliths (or, essenti=
ally, soil) and geopolymers, <a href=3D"https://media.hubspot.com/e3t/Ctc/U=
B+113/d2q-Vf04/VWDJYV540XgfW62JSGb4FrmqyW7TctdS5JmfCPN4nN_cW2-ZW0W7lCdLW6lZ=
3p2W1nK82v1Gg-MqW8zQ8Fy4yzStRW8MSmlQ7ymRZ-W8Nc3lB8TX05KW4yjhTb3XTCCvW8x8fRq=
61_3JxW5Ss8Yl4fV9fYN2RwBT5N6vGYW31xX5554pnChW8CbHd24lx4wpW3Jh-cK5jdWVVW5vtQ=
2M6xVyrZW92k4DF7wjqSdW1GLG_N2cJBTlVjSfQf1csvphW1gJbC83_3y6VN5T58rKMCgXPW2sh=
34J8RvLKmW1C8L7t1tzd73N4_6rZQsq5PMW3Q7q2-6H_7LSVRnMR-2XH_-cW9l-nsY8Hq8R-Vvs=
8Gm6Lwntdf2-5pRd04" style=3D"color:#192733" data-hs-link-id=3D"0" data-hs-l=
ink-id-v2=3D"eRJFAAWa" target=3D"_blank">per</a> <span style=3D"font-style:=
 italic;">Ars Technica</span>.&nbsp;<br><br></li>
<li aria-level=3D"1">For mission II, it=E2=80=99ll deploy a larger inflatab=
le structure into a =E2=80=9Clunar pit=E2=80=9D meant to shield it from ext=
reme temperatures, and scale its resource development.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">Come 2032, the initial version of the hotel, =
an inflatable structure built on Earth and deployed to the moon, will be ab=
le to accommodate up to four guests as well as activities like moonwalking,=
 golfing, and more.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">Though it might not be as worth the money as =
the final iteration: a structure modeled after San Francisco=E2=80=99s Pala=
ce of the Fine Arts and built from those aforementioned moon bricks.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">Its ultimate goal: to help jumpstart the luna=
r economy and bring humanity to =E2=80=9C<a href=3D"https://media.hubspot.c=
om/e3t/Ctc/UB+113/d2q-Vf04/VWDJYV540XgfW62JSGb4FrmqyW7TctdS5JmfCPN4nN_bK2-Z=
W0W50kgx26lZ3nwW3rgZJL7vR9FBW1rZ19D9gd5JMW9jWwrF92CL2mW3HxHJH47GH6bW6NxLSq3=
4xDb_W5PTGd-5LPV45W11GgXn7f6Q1XW8TrY8r3mS1DDW4X3g_Q7T7b-XW5ZBJYd5KcsMMW1ZXV=
8V6pGPwPN4ClGvKSyPzhW3Ft0T0581wrZW4mCYZl9bPN2jN2GXNs2kmQ7MW2PH5Yw5xzrZgf6rv=
3w204" style=3D"color:#192733" data-hs-link-id=3D"0" data-hs-link-id-v2=3D"=
R7Lwh+iF" target=3D"_blank">the next frontier</a>,=E2=80=9D which will even=
tually include Mars.&nbsp;&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%; font-weight:bold; font-size:18px">Sound a bit=
 far-fetched?&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">For sure =E2=80=94 especially when considerin=
g the one-year-old company=E2=80=99s team currently consists of just three =
people, including founder Skyler Chan, who is just 22 years old =E2=80=94 b=
ut, to be fair, so did the idea of sending people to space in 1969.&nbsp;</=
p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">While there=E2=80=99s definitely room for ske=
pticism, GRU has already received backing from Y Combinator, Nvidia, and <a=
 href=3D"https://media.hubspot.com/e3t/Ctc/UB+113/d2q-Vf04/VWDJYV540XgfW62J=
SGb4FrmqyW7TctdS5JmfCPN4nN_db2-ZW0W7Y8-PT6lZ3ngW2z2yZl9hbcStW2tbTg35sfdX6W6=
XN3QG3H718hW8s_pN92HRBxsW2JlFr-2wDvKXVcxmSB1L3GG5W3Sbsz785jJMFW8rkhyx5xQqrL=
W7Tjl6H6cfm4fW5NFNb34H5YfqW6plRTm99cxpyW7VWKG37MGFLMN46tFjZhRsxWW9d2R3w4lkP=
D0N4YPnz-_dXBYW2z6GK96g5CjmW27rdM32C2SlcW7mQHpN18kHMMW7FjVxS1szsgMW2ynhMl6v=
_Nb6W6606bH5CKPLcW2jt6Dm7gKCM7W4RfpJS6f4L4rW4F3Z1v8F5w-RW2Gqb6M25_B7dW5_FMj=
w3w543kf6pm8GK04" style=3D"color:#192733" data-hs-link-id=3D"0" data-hs-lin=
k-id-v2=3D"NMZqxVzF" target=3D"_blank">investors</a> at Anduril and SpaceX,=
 which has to count for something.</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:150%">&nbsp;</p>
